  "question": "1) Background / Context\n\nThe project involves developing a predictive analytics system to estimate \"Forest area (% of land area)\" for 247 countries in 2012. The estimation is based on historical data ranging from 1960 to 2011. The data is stored in a structured database format.\n\n2) Objectives\n\n- Accurately predict the percentage of forest area for each specified country in 2012.\n- Utilize historical data from 1960 to 2011 for prediction.\n\n3) Stakeholders & Users\n\n- Environmental analysts who will use the predictions for research and policy-making.\n- Data scientists responsible for developing and refining the prediction model.\n- Government agencies interested in monitoring and managing forest resources.\n\n4) Functional Descriptions\n\n- Extract and preprocess historical data from the database.\n- Develop a predictive model using machine learning techniques to estimate 2012 forest area percentages based on past data.\n- Validate and evaluate the model's accuracy with appropriate metrics.\n- Provide a user interface for analysts to access predictions and assess data.\n\n5) Non-Functional Descriptions\n\n- Ensure data security and integrity throughout the data processing pipeline.\n- Design the system to handle up to 500 concurrent users querying the predictions.\n- Deliver predictions with a latency of no more than 2 seconds per request.",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: schemabench_0101\nCREATE TABLE `country_forest_history` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `country_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `country_code` char(3) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `year` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `forest_area_percent` decimal(5,2) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  UNIQUE KEY `country_year_unique` (`country_name`,`year`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `forest_area_prediction` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `country_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `country_code` char(3) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `predicted_year` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `predicted_forest_area_percent` decimal(5,2) NOT NULL,\n  `model_version` varchar(100) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `created_at` datetime NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  UNIQUE KEY `country_prediction_unique` (`country_name`,`predicted_year`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
